#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161863 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "2d698f44-e551-58a2-883b-3a992119bd76" :question/math-academy-id "e-9126" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is $S_X = \\{0,1\\},$ the support of $Y$ is $S_Y = \\{0,1\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0),  (0,1),  (1,0),  (1,1) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(1,0)+f(1,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{2}+a+a+\\frac{5}{2}a & =1 \\\\ 5a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161873 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "f2789f6c-11d5-5132-91b3-be65dac4ce24" :question/math-academy-id "e-9203" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\Big( (X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(2,3),(6,1)}) & =P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(6,1)) \\\\  & =f(2,3)+f(6,1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161874 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "01b86f31-f31e-567d-b798-fc0f10a4d0b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9204" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\left( X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\cdot Y\\ge 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,4))+P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07718863-5ab7-5e3a-99e4-01f1021e541f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241241} {:answer/id #uuid "44a39150-b987-5283-81de-03a5014cf0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241796} {:answer/id #uuid "4cddcdb4-bbfc-5b28-b419-6452a624224a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241866} {:answer/id #uuid "a4f23797-ee0b-5f68-a67b-958de019fbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242632} {:answer/id #uuid "fa997fa3-a0fb-5241-a8a8-86d50f1a33a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44a39150-b987-5283-81de-03a5014cf0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241796} :answer-field/id #uuid "85b14364-2c71-5e8e-97dd-c9bc5e008802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4550dc8-a3da-5572-803a-95d868fd5611" :question/math-academy-id "q-109337" :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,2),(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6))+P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039b80b2-527f-56cc-a9bc-ff3bc90ac111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244338} {:answer/id #uu