orked-solution "Using the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=3)=f(0,3)=\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276407a1-c777-5765-92a5-f8ee882f9beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244661} {:answer/id #uuid "498288b9-ed63-5e8c-bab0-3ac6b4c64ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244968} {:answer/id #uuid "7d9c67fe-61e7-5aae-b419-132af9c09f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245417} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d193d8-cb60-5bfa-b6ff-628e2ed9f8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245746} {:answer/id #uuid "d48d0264-007c-539c-bce5-2716b46cb8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "498288b9-ed63-5e8c-bab0-3ac6b4c64ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244968} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b957f2-ea0d-54ac-8727-d392bba73b06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c918d0f-d5e8-53f3-87dc-7849697dc0d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-110935" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in {(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)}) & =P((X,Y)=(1,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,2)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,2)+f(2,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.05+0.05 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42174e88-4fd0-5f22-8ce2-51528ab16a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244892} {:answer/id #uuid "6180d293-576b-5d9e-8020-1cd9c11946d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245164} {:answer/id #uuid "63e729e4-8b82-579f-8666-b74f4b27948e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245192} {:answer/id #uuid "7bbe2490-de04-5bd0-880c-8ecf548fa41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245399} {:answer/id #uuid "da13c233-cb70-55ec-a9f4-82462e7a9dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e729e4-8b82-579f-8666-b74f4b27948e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245192} :answer-field/id #uuid "49e87a25-10c2-5f14-abb0-51d4dc5b16c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93fb8ebd-88df-5ce5-b2be-8dd737a33a7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110937" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in {(3,1),(3,2),(3,3)})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(3,1),(3,2),(3,3)}) & =P((X,Y)=(3,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,3)) \\\\  & =f(3,1)+f(3,2)+f(3,3) \\\\  & =0.05+0.05+0.1 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162073 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172b0d28-9053-5c75-82a3-9176b2177f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423184} {:answer/id #uuid "19dfeb7e-c8d5-5045-9993-de85d2a62535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423185} {:answer/id #uuid "311d7f39-80c9-5bd3-b7a2-7108330abf41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423186} {:answer/id #uuid "80910aba-a6f7-5cea-a000-b98b3f7a7db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423187} {:answer/id #uuid "9c647d4a-3f89-51f3-80fe-0c630dad6a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "172b0d28-9053-5c75-82a3-9176b2177f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423184} :answer-field/id #uuid "80684957-1816-5bbf-b499-0054dfab3f98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9a0e99d-ee2e-54a9-9f59-8e7f0b18bda7" :question/math-academy-id "q-110966" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.01$ | $0.05$ | $0.025$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.025$ | $0.01$ | $0.01$ | $0.025$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.01$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.01$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.025$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCalculate $P(Y-X=2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y-X=2) & =P(X=0,Y=2)+P(X=1,Y=3) \\\\  & +P(X=2,Y=4)+P(X=3,Y=5) \\\\  & =f(0,2)+f(1,3)+f(2,4)+f(3,5) \\\\  & =0.01+0.01+0.1+0.1 \\\\  & =0.22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f3ba5d-e75a-5ecf-a19b-64923cce981a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244362} {:answer/id #uuid "36d0ef4c-2791-5c6a-99b9-b1aa2cd23e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244799} {:answer/id #uuid "56d4fc95-c564-5a8f-9fcb-d46a1dc55b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245078} {:answer/id #uuid "6e279fce-d7a1-5c40-980d-2c4ae52392d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245288} {:answer/id #uuid "79f2e7bf-b778-5573-890d-9c522914975b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e279fce-d7a1-5c40-980d-2c4ae52392d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245288} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5767537-bf21-5ec8-a24b-cbcf91edba98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed526ede-6ba9-5979-b07c-e565cdc8a6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-111076" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(2,5),(4,1),(4,3),(4,5)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,5))+P((X,Y)=(4,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(4,3))+P((X,Y)=(4,5)) \\\\  & =f(2,5)+f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b75537-21fa-5936-a246-9d07783e3b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245088} {:answer/id #uuid "8f58821c-0296-5ea8-a2d2-48043c4716cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245563} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f5673a-0467-5627-a6d5-3d454e5287ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245770} {:answer/id #uuid "a38d072d-7407-51dc-90d8-8e24b0dc2cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245772} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e1ee6f-bd45-58f3-b0da-a2658d8e5629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57b75537-21fa-5936-a246-9d07783e3b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245088} :answer-field/id #uuid "6743a879-72e7-5a72-92ba-9f2e09c241da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b0070a7-d639-52f6-9076-6af2ae611dd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-111081" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.06$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,0),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(1,0)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.15+0.1+0.05+0.1+0.1 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89bddea6-bbe2-51b8-adf4-de306f1c6836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273576} {:answer/id #uuid "8e52a1ab-35d5-5c3f-8591-929097128649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273617} {:answer/id #uuid "94a7a522-7254-5d79-914a-36556eb0b65c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273682} {:answer/id #uuid "b22de866-0abf-5b09-a709-899483e618d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273926} {:answer/id #uuid "ea17a99a-d10e-5140-b7fb-13d127018d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22de866-0abf-5b09-a709-899483e618d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273926} :answer-field/id #uuid "43fbf250-71a6-5396-96bb-258f31270702" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62d0b863-0ebd-5fe2-bf2e-b910931d25fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-143865" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\n- $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n- ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n- $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition I is true. Every value of $f(x,y)$ in the table satisfies $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.4+0.3+0.2+0.1=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is true. Because $f(x,y)$ satisfies conditions I and II, it is a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31f1d221-2dd7-560d-82a2-7d46ae6b176e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272836} {:answer/id #uuid "4213bce1-76c9-5136-a7d9-04e6c02e40b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272951} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6589c3-e359-5255-ba4f-727d02078464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273598} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c65048-82c6-5cb4-9299-4b16e2ea1a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273798} {:answer/id #uuid "c94e4287-a09e-5eb1-b4c8-3b6e1df00892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c6589c3-e359-5255-ba4f-727d02078464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273598} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd7e417-aa58-5703-ab08-b4b4f4c467c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9521225-8707-5e6c-956f-3108e3ec960c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143868" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $-0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $-0.3$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\n- $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n- ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n- $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition I is false. The values of $f(2,1)$ and $f(3,3)$ in the table does not satisfy $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =-0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4+0.6-0.3=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is false. Because $f(x,y)$ does not satisfy condition I, it is *not* a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f7eb31-6717-55c0-b42b-2e49c8af7ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272730} {:answer/id #uuid "62b903b2-02b4-50f3-b1a1-0aab1f492fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273235} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a0bb71-197f-5176-bfed-2c99da1a9204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273939} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fdf346-b652-5601-919c-ae184be3a5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273958} {:answer/id #uuid "ec18b530-7dbe-5d5a-bf3a-20ae46cbbc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f7eb31-6717-55c0-b42b-2e49c8af7ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272730} :answer-field/id #uuid "59d6bbdd-82e4-5cb9-987f-bb953d93ed75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b48a6d92-bb8d-5520-9846-8b67d6784e46" :question/math-academy-id "q-143869" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.16$ | $-0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.24$ | $0.35$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\n- $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n- ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n- $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition I is false. The value of $f(2,2)$ in the table does not satisfy $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.2+0.15+0.16-0.1+0.24+0.35=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is false. Because $f(x,y)$ does not satisfy condition I, it is *not* a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
